## Phase 7: Create Infrastructure (Console)

### Step 1: Create Security Groups

#### ALB Security Group (`flask-alb-sg`)

| Direction | Type | Port | Source |
|-----------|------|------|--------|
| Inbound | HTTPS | 443 | `<YOUR_IP>/32` |
| Inbound | Custom TCP | 8443 | `<YOUR_IP>/32` |
| Outbound | All traffic | All | 0.0.0.0/0 |

#### ECS Task Security Group (`flask-ecs-task-sg`)

| Direction | Type | Port | Source |
|-----------|------|------|--------|
| Inbound | Custom TCP | 8080 | `flask-alb-sg` (select SG) |
| Outbound | All traffic | All | 0.0.0.0/0 |

---

### Step 2: Create Target Groups

#### Production (`flask-tg-blue`)

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Target type | IP |
| Protocol | **HTTP** |
| Port | **8080** |
| VPC | Your VPC |
| Health check protocol | HTTP |
| Health check path | `/health` |
| Health check port | 8080 |

#### Test (`flask-tg-green`)

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Target type | IP |
| Protocol | **HTTP** |
| Port | **8080** |
| VPC | Your VPC |
| Health check protocol | HTTP |
| Health check path | `/health` |
| Health check port | 8080 |

> ⚠️ **Critical:** Protocol MUST be HTTP. Containers don't have TLS — ALB handles TLS termination.

---

### Step 3: Import SSL Certificate

```bash
openssl req -x509 -nodes -days 365 -newkey rsa:2048 \
  -keyout server.key -out server.crt \
  -subj "/CN=flask-app.example.com/O=krisha"

aws acm import-certificate --region us-west-2 \
  --certificate fileb://server.crt \
  --private-key fileb://server.key
```

> Use FQDN format (e.g. `flask-app.example.com`) — ALB rejects certs without proper domain.

